TeaVM Compatibility Libraries

Elemental2 and JsInterop APIs originate with Google and their contributors, under
Apache License 2.0. The build resolves the declared Elemental2 artifacts from Maven;
generated adaptations retain their original source headers.

The modular GWT service compatibility sources retain the original package names
and copyright headers of the APIs they adapt.

The GWT client compatibility implementation and portable contracts were extracted
from the bootstrap-widgets project (https://github.com/instanto-io/bootstrap-widgets).
Sources retain their Google,
GWT and other original contributor headers. Independent TeaVM adaptations are
maintained under io.instanto, without claiming upstream ownership or endorsement.

The GWT client additions include maintained GWT 2.13.1 source for editors, text
direction, event buses, HTML sanitisation, stylesheet batching, position results
and typed-array contracts. Original headers remain in source; provenance/gwt-*
records the upstream source hashes and adaptation notes.

The UiBinder compatibility processor was extracted from the Bootstrap widget
project, Copyright (C) 2026 Carl Stainton, under Apache License 2.0. It includes
Material-driven generic setter, preformatted text and default-string generation.

The GWT resource compatibility Maven plugin was extracted from the Bootstrap
widget project, Copyright (C) 2026 Carl Stainton, under Apache License 2.0.
The imported files and source revision are recorded in
provenance/gwt-resources-compat-maven-plugin.json.
